+
+2026-06-25 fix/incomplete-data-null — universal incomplete-data->NULL task. The RULE is LOCKED (every metric, team AND player, is NULL when its inputs are not 100% available across the window; recorded 2026-06-25 above). Two REACH/CONSEQUENCE questions raised BLINDED (working_agreement §11, two paths each, no recommendation) BEFORE writing any model — they set the blast radius, not the rule. Both put to the CPO in plain language (AskUserQuestion, 2026-06-25):
+  (Q1 — reach to counts/per-90s) Does the rule apply to COUNT totals (a player's season goals/shots/tackles that drive the leaderboards; any team stat-sum totals shown as counts) and PER-90s too, or only to per-match averages + ratios? Path A = include counts + per-90s (maximally consistent; any entity with one uncovered window game drops off the count leaderboards / loses its per-90s — boards can be sparse early-season / low-coverage). Path B = only averages + ratios (counts/per-90s stay honest best-effort sums; leaderboards stay populated but totals can understate uncovered players + aren't strictly comparable).
+      CPO ANSWER (AskUserQuestion, 2026-06-25): **Path A — include counts + per-90s.** Every stats-based metric NULLs on any uncovered window game; count totals and per-90s included. The leaderboard drop-off (handled by mart_leaderboards' existing `where <metric> > 0`, which excludes a NULL count) is the accepted, intended consequence.
+  (Q2 — #320 reversal) Confirm this deliberately REVERSES the #320 "average over the covered games (+ caption)" design for the TEAM per-match rates (they go NULL on any partial coverage instead of averaging over the covered subset). Path A = reverse #320 (consistent; partial-window team averages become '—'; moves live numbers). Path B = keep #320 for team rates (stays populated but the codebase keeps two incompleteness rules — the inconsistency this task removes).
+      CPO ANSWER (AskUserQuestion, 2026-06-25): **Path A — reverse #320.** Team per-match rates NULL on partial coverage; this is a deliberate, recorded reversal of the #320 same-window-average design (the marts today divide each rate by its coverage count — games_with_team_stats / games_with_sot_stats / games_with_opp_stats / games_with_player_stats — and the change ALSO gates: NULL when that count < the window total). Scoreline-based metrics (goals/points/W-D-L/clean sheets) stay always-covered → never NULL from this rule.
+
+2026-06-25 fix/incomplete-data-null — PREMISE CORRECTION (player side) + CPO ruling, BEFORE any model code. The spec said the player models "coalesce missing per-game stats to 0 and compute anyway" and prescribed adding per-stat coverage counts (countif(field is not null)) gated vs appearances. A source-of-record check (read-only BQ, per Appendix A6 "measure before asserting") REFUTED that premise:
+  - Player stat nulls predominantly mean ZERO, not missing: of 1.29M player rows with minutes>0, 91.7% have null goals_total; saves null 95.1% overall. (Team stat nulls, by contrast, are 0.6-3.7% → genuinely missing.)
+  - PROOF via ground truth (the scoreline): summing player goals_total (null→0) per team-fixture reconciles EXACTLY with the actual match score in 95.88% of the 85,738 finished team-fixtures that have player data (~all the rest off by exactly 1 = own goals, which aren't in any player's goals_total). If null meant "missing", this reconciliation would be near-zero. So null=zero is proven; each recorded player appearance is COMPLETE and coalesce-to-0 is correct.
+  - Concrete example: a Liverpool 4-goal match — Mané 2 + Salah 1 + Sturridge 1 = 4 = score; every other player's goals = null while playing ~90 min with full passing data (null = didn't score, not missing).
+  - The genuine player incompleteness is FIXTURE-LEVEL: 21,246 of 106,984 finished team-fixtures (19.9%) have NO player data at all.
+  So the spec's per-FIELD player coverage gate would NULL ~92% of players (empty leaderboards) — invalid. Put to the CPO with the evidence + the concrete example (no anchoring).
+      CPO RULING (conversation, 2026-06-25): "So for player treat NULL as zero is correct? Do it." → the PLAYER models are LEFT AS-IS (null=zero / coalesce-to-0 is correct); the per-field player gate is DROPPED. The ~20%-of-matches fixture-level player-data gap is LEFT ALONE (not handled in this task). The TEAM side proceeds unchanged (team stat nulls genuinely = missing): reverse #320 — NULL team per-match rates + stat-count totals + the team player-DERIVED per-match metrics (key_passes/tackles/duels — these inherit the fixture-level player-data gap, tracked by games_with_player_stats) on partial coverage. Q1 (include counts + per-90s) now applies to the TEAM stat-count totals only. The task is therefore TEAM-ONLY.
